<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Leo IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/855">855</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leo IV was pope from 847 to 855. Elected after Muslim raiders had sacked the basilica of Saint Peter in 846, he enclosed the Vatican hill with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonine-wall">Leonine Wall</a>, creating the fortified Leonine City, and organised the alliance of southern Italian cities whose fleet defeated another raid at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ostia">Battle of Ostia</a> in 849. He also restored churches damaged in the raid.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-leo-iv.jpg" alt="Pope Leo IV" width="320" height="521" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PalauanLibertarian · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PopeLeoIV_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After Arab raiders sacked the basilica of Saint Peter in 846, <b>Leo IV</b> enclosed the Vatican with the Leonine Wall, and a papal-allied fleet defeated another Arab force at the Battle of Ostia in 849.</blockquote><a href="/empire/papal-states">Papal States · Military</a></li></ul></section>
